# AutoNumber Name Field With a BLANK Display Format = HARD BLOCKER (PARK, never guess)

When an object's standard **`Name`** field is declared as **AutoNumber** on the
sheet (object-meta `Name Field Type` = `Autonumber`) but its **display format**
(`Name Field Display Format`) is **BLANK**, the object is **un-deployable** and
MUST be treated as a Step-0 blocker. Salesforce REJECTS a CustomObject whose
`<nameField>` is AutoNumber with no `displayFormat`, so neither a create nor an
update of that object can succeed until a format is supplied.

This applies to NEW objects (create) AND to existing objects whose Name is being
changed to AutoNumber.

## Why this rule exists (real incident, 2026-09-09)

The new object `TI_Fnt_ExportControlClassification__c` declared `Name =
AutoNumber` with an empty display format. It could not be created. It was parked
(flagged, not deployed) while the sibling objects (`AppendedTableMaster`,
`ContainerCertificate`, `ConditionsPerformanceReport`) deployed normally.

## Required behavior (every object, every run)

1. **Detect at Step-0.** While scanning the object-meta block (live, per
   `read-sheet-live.mdc`), if `Name Field Type` is AutoNumber and
   `Name Field Display Format` is blank → this is a HARD `ERROR` blocker for the
   WHOLE object.
2. **PARK the object — do NOT deploy it.** Exclude it from the deploy set. Other
   objects in the same batch that are clean still deploy.
3. **Flag it via `flag_blocker.py`** (coupled AH note + Col-A highlight) on the
   object's lead field row, with a message stating the object is parked because
   its AutoNumber Name field has a blank display format, pending the sheet
   owner's decision. Also set the affected fields' AI `Deployment Status` to
   `Not Deployed`.
4. **NEVER auto-generate or guess the display format.** This is the key
   distinction from a blank FORMULA body (which IS auto-filled with a
   return-type dummy per `sf-deploy-delta-and-blockers.mdc`): a Name numbering
   scheme (prefix + width, e.g. `ECC-{0000000000}`) is a business/client
   decision. Fabricating one would permanently mis-number every record. Ask the
   sheet owner (e.g. Yagai-san) for the exact format.
5. **When the format arrives:** write it into the object-meta display-format cell
   (gated sheet write, per `sheet-write-confirmation.mdc`), then deploy the
   CustomObject and verify live.

## Guardrails

- A blank AutoNumber display format is a HARD blocker, not a warning — never let
  such an object into the package.
- Reads are LIVE; the flag is coupled (AH + Col-A) via `flag_blocker.py`.
- Do not confuse this with the empty-formula auto-dummy behavior — formulas get a
  safe dummy, AutoNumber Name formats never do.
- Text Name fields and AutoNumber Name fields WITH a valid format are fine and
  deploy normally.
